      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked the run as UNKNOWN, not NORMAL, and asked for a human to review it. Every installed sensor looks fine, but growth requires a tube pressure gauge and this furnace doesn't have one.\n\n- **Readings so far:** temperature is holding at 750 °C within about 1 °C, after a brief 10 °C overshoot at the start of growth. Heater power is steady at 44–46%. Argon flow is on setpoint at about 100 sccm. The controller reports no faults.\n- **Oxygen:** exhaust O2 has stayed at 3.5–7 ppm since the purge, which rules out a leaky seal letting air in.\n- **The gap:** without a pressure reading, a blocked exhaust wouldn't show up on any installed sensor. The argon flow meter is under active control, so it would keep reading about 100 sccm anyway, and O2 wouldn't necessarily rise.\n- **Results:** there are no measurements of the sample yet, so there's nothing to say about whether the material grew.\n\nA person needs to decide whether to go on without the pressure gauge, or to check the exhaust line by some other means."
     }
